From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add Time-Of-Day-Condition's omitted members

RFC 5777's verified erratum 2333 (section 4.2.1): "3 AVPs are omitted
in the ABNF for the Time-Of-Day-Condition AVP". Its corrected ABNF adds
Absolute-Start-Fractional-Seconds after Absolute-Start-Time,
Absolute-End-Fractional-Seconds after Absolute-End-Time and
Timezone-Offset after Timezone-Flag. The dictionary already has the
three (567, 569, 571, clauses 4.2.8, 4.2.10 and 4.2.12); only the
group's member list follows the uncorrected ABNF.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..66eb06d 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -2641,8 +2641,11 @@
 				<gavp name="Day-Of-Month-Mask"/>
 				<gavp name="Month-Of-Year-Mask"/>
 				<gavp name="Absolute-Start-Time"/>
+				<gavp name="Absolute-Start-Fractional-Seconds"/>
 				<gavp name="Absolute-End-Time"/>
+				<gavp name="Absolute-End-Fractional-Seconds"/>
 				<gavp name="Timezone-Flag"/>
+				<gavp name="Timezone-Offset"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
 		<avp name="Time-Of-Day-Start" code="561" mandatory="may">
